  "body": {
    "id": "prop:rank-one-endpoint",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Assume \\(\\mathcal M_{T_0,T_1}(0)\\ne\\varnothing\\). In the admissible specialization \\(N=3,r=s=1\\), \\(\\kappa_\\star=1/\\sqrt3\\). For every nonempty endpoint stratum \\(\\mathcal M_{T_0,T_1}(1/\\sqrt3)\\), if \\(T_0\\ge\\overline T\\), the decision program \\(\\widehat{\\mathcal C}_{\\mathrm{end}}\\) satisfies \\(\\inf_{\\vartheta\\in\\mathcal M_{T_0,T_1}(1/\\sqrt3)}\\Pr_\\vartheta\\{\\beta\\in\\widehat{\\mathcal C}_{\\mathrm{end}}\\}\\ge1-\\alpha\\) and, on every data realization, \\(\\operatorname{diam}_2(\\widehat{\\mathcal C}_{\\mathrm{end}})\\le\\min\\{2B,2\\sqrt3\\varepsilon_1\\}\\). Consequently, uniformly in \\(T_1\\ge1\\), \\(R_{\\mathrm{or}}(1/\\sqrt3)\\asymp\\min\\{B,T_1^{-1/2}\\}\\), whereas \\(R_{\\mathrm{ad}}(1/\\sqrt3)\\asymp\\rho_{\\mathrm{ad}}(1/\\sqrt3)\\). The event \\(\\widehat h\\ne h\\) uses the reserved \\(\\alpha/2\\) noncoverage budget and contributes no additive expected-diameter term because the displayed diameter bound is pathwise for every selected line.",
